# The record and allow files, by tools/record_merge.py's CLASSES (a test holds this file to it; #6375). Two PRs
# appending a row to one assumptions table, or an entry to one package's mutgate record, keep both on a local merge.
# A line both add word for word is one line to every reader (#6358); doclint, mutgate and premerge fail one ID or
# mutant key on two different lines, and premerge reads an entry the union brought back as changed. Allow files
# take no union: it could bring back a line one side removed. Every class is LF text, so git commits a CRLF line as
# its LF twin, and doclint, mutgate and the driver refuse a carriage return that reached a commit another way.
# GitHub's server-side merge ignores this file (agents merge main locally). A clone that ran
# `tools/record_merge.py --install` merges every class by key instead (info/attributes), so an edited line is not
# kept twice and an identical one is kept once; CI and premerge's replay keep the union.
ASSUMPTIONS.md merge=union text eol=lf
MUTANTS-EQUIVALENT merge=union text eol=lf
*_allow.txt text eol=lf
*.allow text eol=lf
allow*.txt text eol=lf
